# SafeEdge — Probability models

`PoissonFootballProbabilityModel` is the frozen v1 baseline. Do not change its semantics to make a later model look better.

v2 is `RegularizedDixonColesFootballProbabilityModel`. v3 is `JointDixonColesFootballProbabilityModel`. All implement `FootballProbabilityModel`. Walk-forward orchestration selects the model. Do not branch on model version inside CandidateEngine, StrategyEngine, BacktestEngine, or SettlementEngine.

Do not mutate v1 or v2 to make v3 look better. Do not silently fall back from v3 to v1/v2.

## Development vs validation

Probability-model development and diagnostic tuning use only Premier League, Bundesliga, and Serie A.

La Liga and Ligue 1 are reserved later validation. Do not run them, inspect them, or import new diagnostics for them during model development.

## Fitting rules

Bookmaker odds are never features of the score model and never enter ρ, shrinkage, attack/defence, or other score-model fitting.

Betting ROI, candidate edge, and strategy results never fit ρ, shrinkage, regularization, half-life, or other score-model parameters.

Evaluate model changes on edge ranking, settlement calibration, score likelihood, and confidence compression. Do not treat ROI alone as success or failure.

When uncertain, stop rather than leaking market prices into the score model.
